---
description: >-
  Bottom-to-top gitgraph where branch1 accumulates more commits than main
  between its branch point and merge back into main, causing commits from
  the two branches to land at overlapping vertical positions - a layout
  stress test for overlapping commits in BT orientation.
---
gitGraph BT:
  commit id:"s1"
  commit id:"s2"
  branch branch1
  commit id:"s3"
  commit id:"s4"
  checkout main
  commit id:"s5"
  checkout branch1
  commit id:"s6"
  commit id:"s7"
  merge main
